A||N||8||SloPonti||need help with the holley aftermarket throttle body for the 2.5 from summit||||13||
Z||000000||SloPonti||04-13-2000||11:41 PM||||i called to order the holley throttle body for the 2.5-there price is 251 bucks for it-not to bad but they do not guarentee it to fit and they will not return it! in fact they said they would rather not sell it to me! he explained to me but i did not understand why! does anyone no what they are talking about! or could one of you guys call them and find out what they meen! the part number is 500-1.  i want to buy this because my motor has been modified and the only part i havn't touched is the throttle body plus i have the hooker header and holley says it works well with it!<BR>let me know and thanks!<BR>Rob||||reg||13
Z||000001||Racer 1||04-14-2000||01:03 AM||||Holley used to make aluminum intake manifold also. Call Holley carbs direct and ask them as far as I know everthing was a plug and play setup. But see I think the holley intake and carb was supposed to go together. Because you throttle diameter isnt going to be any bigger. Because your stock intake manifold opening is the same size as the stock TBI throat. So there might be a problem then. good luck||||reg||10
Z||000002||2FAST4U||04-14-2000||01:16 AM||||I have a Holley TB on one of my 2.5s and it works great. I have heard of some problems with throttle plate interference but that was easily corrected with a drill and flapper wheel on the manifold mounting flange. I probably didn't have this problem because my manifold has been flowed and ported already. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||fotofrank||04-15-2000||01:18 AM||||Hate to break your heart but I got a used Holley TBI on the net for $85.00.<BR>I spent the last hour or so opening up the input manifold so the throtle plate would clear it. It seems to me that if you don't open the input where the TBI mounts you loose much of the advantage of the bigger TBI. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">||||reg||11
Z||000004||theogre||04-15-2000||03:54 PM||||From what I've been able to dig out about this..... it should fit. Like they said above you may need to do some intake work. <P>the intake work isn't hard. stuff a rag down each runner then vacuum out all the waste. Open the intake to match the TBI base.<P>Ideally you want to port the head if that hasn't been done yet.||||reg||1
Z||000005||SloPonti||04-16-2000||01:20 AM||||well i did get it ordered finally through summit for 250.00! rumor from summit is that this model is going to be discontinued! well anyways it is on the way! i am not quite sure on what i need to do to make it work-the fiero store says it should fit with no problems but some of you guys are saying different-anyone have pictures of what i need to do!<BR>thanks<BR>Rob||||reg||1
Z||000006||SloPonti||04-17-2000||09:32 PM||||someone help me out here!<BR>thanks<BR>Rob||||reg||1
Z||000007||HF6582||04-18-2000||02:28 AM||||Slo,<BR>I don't think I have the Holley paper work anymore, but in a nutshell this is what they say to do.<P>To make the TBI fit you have to enlarge the throttle opening on the stock manifold to the size of the TBI opening.<P>Be very carefull not to go to far back into the EGR port work. <P>You will be able to see how big when you get your TBI.<P>Scott||||reg||1
Z||000008||fotofrank||04-18-2000||01:43 PM||||If you get a Holley TBI spacer and gasket with your TBI you may be all set. When I got mine(used) I got nothing but the TBI. I had to open the hole in the spacer and gasket(new stock parts) to allow the flapper or butterfly valve to open. It is not nessesary to have the opening perfectly round sonce turbulance of air/fule makes for better combining of air/fuel for detonation. When you remove the stock TBI you may find a deflector plat in the intake. From the Holley instructions do you leave this in or remove it? I reinstalled mine in a ported intake.||||reg||11
